{{!-- The Gmail API scopes an app in `baseScopes: api` mode requests, as list items. Shared by the
interactive `gmail` block and the `gmailService` one: what an app asks Google for follows from its own
scope selection, not from whether a person or a service account presents it. A service-account app
listing gmail.modify here while it had deliberately skipped it is the bug this partial exists to stop
coming back. --}}

{{#unless disabledScopes.Gmail_Modify}}
<li><code>"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify"</code></li>
{{else}}
{{#if isSendOnlyGmail}}
<li><code>"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send"</code></li>
{{else}}
<li><code>"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly"</code></li>
<li><code>"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.labels"</code></li>
{{/if}}
{{/unless}}
